{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks","id":1548773,"title":"Dodging magickal attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-25T18:21:51-08:00","id":1548773,"title":"Dodging magickal attacks","content":"I know that this have been extensively discussed, buy I could never get a definitive answer and better yet, I could never make sense of the phrasing of M20 (a very hard feat)<br /> <br /> So, we have a bunch of ink about casting magickal attacks on M20.<br /> <br /> Since we all know and have no issue with regular magickal attacks like: plasma guns, enhanced fists, thrown objects (<b>thrown</b> fireball), as they all require a specific att+ability to hit, and they have to travel a distance to the target, making it possible for the target to dodge, we don't need to cover that. <br /> <br /> My questions are about oyher kinds of effects, like: curses, spontaneous combustions, lightning strikes or remd the body.<br /> <br /> So, M20 p.544 has this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any physical attack (fireball, mystic blade, plasma bolt, etc.) directed at an essentially solid target (car, person, spirit, etc.) can be dodged if that target is capable of dodging the attack in question. As detailed under Chapter Nine\u2019s Combat section, a Dexterity + Athletics (or Acrobatics) roll, difficulty 6, subtracts successes from an incoming attack. If the attacker still has more successes than the target, remaining successes determine how much damage is done\u2026 and if the attacker winds up with only one success left over, then there\u2019s no damage at all. Really obvious attacks \u2013 lightning bolts, clouds of deadly gas, and so forth \u2013 are easy to see coming. Invisible ones \u2013 flesh-eating spirits, silent curses, Entropic ripples that collapse a bridge, that sort of thing \u2013 may be detected with a successful Perception + Awareness roll, difficulty 8. </div> </div> </div>So, you can only dodge attacks which you are capable to detect and capable to dodge.<br /> <br /> Question: Does the awareness roll provides enough information to allow the target to dodge? I mean, if someone chants a bunch of words and suddenly a lightning comes down grom the sky, how does the target knows where to jump beforehand (as no one would dodge the lightning after it shoots, the target have to jump before, just like &quot;dodging&quot; bullets)?<br /> <br /> If awareness does grant this info (&quot;you feel energh building on top of you which will form a lightning strike&quot;), then that is top quality precog. An overpowered spider-sense for an ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, regarding magickal attacks that does not a\u00e7lows dodge. <br /> <br /> In M20 p.417 we have:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Focused Magick: If that attack uses a normal attack \u2013 like a punch or death-ray cannon \u2013 as a focus instrument,, the attacker needs to make a successful Dexterity + appropriate combat Ability roll. An Arete roll decides the success or failure of the magick, and the attack roll determines whether or not it hit the target. Such attacks, as mentioned earlier, can be dodged<br /> .<br /> \u2022 Openly Magickal: If the attack is itself magickal \u2013 like a lightning bolt, incendiary gesture, transformation blast, or flesh-shredding curse of pure hate \u2013 then the assailant rolls her Arete as an attack roll instead. Such attacks are almost always vulgar and can be as dangerous to their originators as to their victims.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Indirect Assault: If the attack is indirect \u2013 an earthquake, poison, an Entropy-weakened scaffolding, and so on \u2013 then the attacker rolls her Arete as above, but the attack is often coincidental rather than vulgar. This might be the most common tactic in the Awakened arsenal, especially since it\u2019s rarely obvious enough to note until later. </div> </div> </div>Notice that in a focused magick attack, it's directly stated that it allows dodge. And according to BoS Faq, successes of the attack roll does not carry on to damage like regular attacks.<br /> <br /> In an openly magickal attacks, it isn't stated that dosge is allowed. However, they tend to be vulgar.<br /> <br /> Is that the only advantage of a focused magick attack? Being coincident?<br /> <br /> Also, indirect assaults seem to be both coincident *and* not allow dodge. So it has no cons. Any reason to not always use that one?<br /> <br /> Since what differenciates those kinds of attacks is merely how the mage wants to create his effect, why not use the no sodge, coincident one?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T08:10:04-08:00","id":1548785,"title":"","content":"A lot of this depends on how rules bound we are. Indirect attacks look like they can't be noticed, but I think that really means they are harder to notice. Looking at the indirect attack examples, I see a mix of situations. <br /> <br /> The collapsing scaffold is equivalent to the collapsing bridge mentioned earlier. It's an essentially physical attack (collapsing scaffold) directed at a target (whatever is under it) so with the Perception + Awareness roll, it can be dodged. <br /> <br /> The poison depends greatly on delivery method. If it is the equivalent of clouds of deadly gas from earlier it may be obvious. Whether it can be dodged will then depend on if the person even has the capacity. Dodge in this case may mean getting a gas mask on quickly enough, and if you don't have a gas mask you can't dodge.<br /> <br /> The earthquake is unnoticeable only in the sense that people can't tell it was done by magic. If it is large enough to cause damage, people are definitely noticing it. It is also undodgeable in the sense that it is everywhere, but falling debris and other specific effects are potentially dodgeable if they are noticed in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T12:16:36-08:00","id":1548795,"title":"","content":"I always rule that attacks you have to target have to hit as in the examples above.<br /> Attacks that autohit require pattern locking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T15:26:59-08:00","id":1548796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548785#post1548785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of this depends on how rules bound we are. Indirect attacks look like they can't be noticed, but I think that really means they are harder to notice. Looking at the indirect attack examples, I see a mix of situations.<br /> <br /> The collapsing scaffold is equivalent to the collapsing bridge mentioned earlier. It's an essentially physical attack (collapsing scaffold) directed at a target (whatever is under it) so with the Perception + Awareness roll, it can be dodged.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I made my first question. I'm not sure awareness grants enough information (like the scaffold will fall over you), but only a sense of &quot;magick is being used around&quot;. Which would make the target unable to dodge, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The poison depends greatly on delivery method. If it is the equivalent of clouds of deadly gas from earlier it may be obvious. Whether it can be dodged will then depend on if the person even has the capacity. Dodge in this case may mean getting a gas mask on quickly enough, and if you don't have a gas mask you can't dodge. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they didn't say how the poison is going to be applied. Only that it is coincident. So maybe the con of this method is that it's harder to apply? Or you need environment stuff (like the scaffold)?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> That would be my next question. You can make an attack unavoidable by combining another sphere, right? But unless you want the effect to constantly follow the target (which isn't true with a single turn direct damage spell) wouldn't you need just one sphere rank 1 for detection? Like Life 1 to detect that person pattern?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T16:39:29-08:00","id":1548799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548796#post1548796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be my next question. You can make an attack unavoidable by combining another sphere, right? But unless you want the effect to constantly follow the target (which isn't true with a single turn direct damage spell) wouldn't you need just one sphere rank 1 for detection? Like Life 1 to detect that person pattern?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be generaly true for all locking effects. But all the data claims locking is higher usually at 2. I also assume to autohit you have to not detect but lock the effect on the more or less moving target.<br /> One of my fav spells is casting a direct line of one way magnetic field between my mages hands and the target (locked effect) and after that casting autohiting lightnings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T08:53:02-08:00","id":1548817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548796#post1548796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I made my first question. I'm not sure awareness grants enough information (like the scaffold will fall over you), but only a sense of &quot;magick is being used around&quot;. Which would make the target unable to dodge, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but for collapsing scaffolds and other events which people can notice and react to with their physical senses Alertness should work. We're not locked to Perception + Awareness just because the book says so. If, however, you think they need the advance notice of 'feeling' a spell, then indeed we are limited to Awareness.<br /> <br /> On a technical level we might say that Awareness lets someone know that magic is happening and Alertness lets them spot what it is. I wouldn't make them roll both, though, because that will just slow the game down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, they didn't say how the poison is going to be applied. Only that it is coincident. So maybe the con of this method is that it's harder to apply? Or you need environment stuff (like the scaffold)? </div> </div> </div>Coincidental magic is indeed harder to apply. Really, though, I think we should answer questions about dodging based on the narrative of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> That would be my next question. You can make an attack unavoidable by combining another sphere, right? But unless you want the effect to constantly follow the target (which isn't true with a single turn direct damage spell) wouldn't you need just one sphere rank 1 for detection? Like Life 1 to detect that person pattern? </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> My standard is that whenever a mage needs a spell to 'see' or 'detect' a thing, it is one step harder than the mage being able to see or detect that thing. That almost always works out to rank 2, one step higher than basic sensory effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-28-2025, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T16:40:00-08:00","id":1548832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> , yeah, locking effects require rank 2 spheres. If you want to lock an effect on an object, you need Matter 2, while locking on a person would be Life 2. However, I insist, locking\u2260detecting. Locking require rank 2 of the target pattern, while detecting should require rank 1 of what you want to detect.<br /> <br /> For example, if you want to cast a spell that makes anyone that has an orange aura (fear) in an area to sleep, you would need Life 3 (for the sleep spell) and Spirit 1, Mind 1 or Life 1+Prime 1 (for reading the aura). You wouldn't need Life 2 (which is the requirement for locking an effect on a person). Don't you agree?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548817#post1548817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but for collapsing scaffolds and other events which people can notice and react to with their physical senses Alertness should work. We're not locked to Perception + Awareness just because the book says so. If, however, you think they need the advance notice of 'feeling' a spell, then indeed we are limited to Awareness.<br /> <br /> On a technical level we might say that Awareness lets someone know that magic is happening and Alertness lets them spot what it is. I wouldn't make them roll both, though, because that will just slow the game down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alertness shouldn't let you know what the spell is going to do. Alertness is only for mundane stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm ok with alertness being rolled to see a scaffold falling. But it's weird to me awareness doing the same for spells, because you don't know how fast the spell is. I mean a scaffolding falling is fast, but it's not speed of light fast. You can look at it and jump. How do you dodge a laser or lightning <b>without knowing what is coming</b> beforehand? (Notice that awareness does not grant that kind of information)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coincidental magic is indeed harder to apply. Really, though, I think we should answer questions about dodging based on the narrative of the game. </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? That this would vary according to the spell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My standard is that whenever a mage needs a spell to 'see' or 'detect' a thing, it is one step harder than the mage being able to see or detect that thing. That almost always works out to rank 2, one step higher than basic sensory effects. </div> </div> </div>Hm, any reason for that? Is there any raw rote or something that backs that up, or you mean as a house rule?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T05:52:57-08:00","id":1548844,"title":"","content":"I also insist that locking may not be the same as detecting but targeting = locking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T16:03:01-08:00","id":1548853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548844#post1548844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also insist that locking may not be the same as detecting but targeting = locking.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Do you have any text in raw or rote to base that argument? Tbh M20 does not have anything (that I can remember) about targeting. <br /> It seems that, in M20, it deepens on howbyou build your spell, as I posted in OP.<br /> If you make it as a gun like the &quot;focused attack options&quot; you have to roll for attack. If you make it an openly magickal attack, you don't have to attack (although they seem to be always vulgar). I can't think of any other advantage of making it an attack, other than making it coincident (if you can), since BoS already said that you don't carry over attacks successes to damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T16:06:09-08:00","id":1548854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548853#post1548853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? Do you have any text in raw or rote to base that argument? Tbh M20 does not have anything (that I can remember) about targeting.<br /> It seems that, in M20, it deepens on howbyou build your spell, as I posted in OP.<br /> If you make it as a gun like the &quot;focused attack options&quot; you have to roll for attack. If you make it an openly magickal attack, you don't have to attack (although they seem to be always vulgar). I can't think of any other advantage of making it an attack, other than making it coincident (if you can), since BoS already said that you don't carry over attacks successes to damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there is little data on the subject so nor my nor your way can be proven. Logicaly detecting would still require you to hit as the target can move.. Locking lets you hit automatically.<br /> The implied advantage is that you do not spend successes on locking. It is also a paradigm thing not everyone can just cast spells on people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-01-2025, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T07:56:30-08:00","id":1548878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548854#post1548854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes there is little data on the subject so nor my nor your way can be proven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The best we can do is try to use logic and examples to reach for an answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548854#post1548854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logicaly detecting would still require you to hit as the target can move..</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you require an attack roll for my example spell I posted before? The one that detects auras in an area and puts anyone with orange aura to sleep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Locking lets you hit automatically.<br /> The implied advantage is that you do not spend successes on locking. It is also a paradigm thing not everyone can just cast spells on people. </div> </div> </div>Wdym? You never spend successes on locking. Locking is just the need of rank 2 of the pattern sphere of the target that you want to affect with an lasting effect. In fact, locking are only for lingering effects, as per M20 p.511<br /> <br /> <br /> If we think about how evey other effect is made in Mage, we will see that no spell requires an attack roll, other then the ones that works like weapons (or hand-to-hand). You see, when you cast a Mind spell to erase someone's memory, you don't have to &quot;hit&quot; the target for the spell to work, right? You just need the target to be in sensory range and roll Arete.The same for Life effects, if you want to change the mood of a person, you don't have to roll attack. You roll Arete and that's it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, rend the body (Life 3) also doesn't require an attack roll. The only time we see a spell requiring attack rolls are spells that are thrown or shot somehow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T09:07:52-08:00","id":1548879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548878#post1548878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Would you require an attack roll for my example spell I posted before? The one that detects auras in an area and puts anyone with orange aura to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No cause thats an area spell, but i would allow someone to dodge it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548879#post1548879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wdym? You never spend successes on locking. Locking is just the need of rank 2 of the pattern sphere of the target that you want to affect with an lasting effect. In fact, locking are only for lingering effects, as per M20 p.511<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere does it say if you spend or do not spend successes on locking (the whole mechanic is badly defined. But logic would suggest that if something is an auto hit it should be harder to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1548867-gene-hackman-and-michelle-trachtenberg-rip?p=1548880#post1548880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we think about how evey other effect is made in Mage, we will see that no spell requires an attack roll, other then the ones that works like weapons (or hand-to-hand). You see, when you cast a Mind spell to erase someone's memory, you don't have to &quot;hit&quot; the target for the spell to work, right? You just need the target to be in sensory range and roll Arete.The same for Life effects, if you want to change the mood of a person, you don't have to roll attack. You roll Arete and that's it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, rend the body (Life 3) also doesn't require an attack roll. The only time we see a spell requiring attack rolls are spells that are thrown or shot somehow...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Body rend is a spell that in my opinion is already locking the target (or its used via touch and that requires a attack)<br /> Lightning and other spells of this kind can use the arete roll as an attack, and that can be dodged. You cant dodge a locked spell.<br /> With mind spells you have to lock someones mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-02-2025, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T13:47:30-08:00","id":1548890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548879#post1548879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No cause thats an area spell, but i would allow someone to dodge it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. What would the attacker roll? What exactly would the target dodge from? Also, it's a duration spell, the mage who casted it could be in a whole different country, so it makes no sense to roll an attack hit.<br /> <br /> PS: Or by dodging you mean avoiding the area? If that's the case (and the target must somehow know that the are has magick on it), then it's ok, but that isn't really a dodge. I mean, there is no dodge after the target enters the area<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548879#post1548879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere does it say if you spend or do not spend successes on locking (the whole mechanic is badly defined. But logic would suggest that if something is an auto hit it should be harder to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 is pretty clear in p.511, that if you want to lock a <b>lingering</b>, <b>mobile</b> Effect into a specific patter, you just need to add that pattern sphere. That's it. But my point was that you don't lock instant effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548879#post1548879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Body rend is a spell that in my opinion is already locking the target (or its used via touch and that requires a attack)<br /> Lightning and other spells of this kind can use the arete roll as an attack, and that can be dodged. You cant dodge a locked spell.<br /> With mind spells you have to lock someones mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I realized after posting that wasn't a good example since it already has Life (which would be the requirement for locking), but the Mind effect is a good one. To lock an effect into someone's Mind, you would need Life, since Mind isn't a pattern sphere. So, if you want to cast an erasing memory spell on someone, you would require Mind+Life? And Mind only would need an attack roll? Makes no sense to me, never seen any of the sort.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Likewise, you want to cast a spell to levitate your target high in the air, you don't need Life (or any other pattern sphere combination for night-folk). You just use Forces 2 to do that. And you also do not roll an attack.<br /> <br /> To be honest, across editions, mages were capable to affect reality anywhere inside their sensory range (with Correspondence increasing that range). In fact, in M20 p.543, where it talks about range, there are no signs of an attack roll being needed to cast a spell. If the target has some sort of cover, though, you get an increase in difficulty on the Arete roll.<br /> The only time an attack is required seems to be when things are thrown or shot. Idk why M20 made such a mess explaining that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 03-02-2025, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T15:52:10-08:00","id":1548892,"title":"","content":"1. If ist just an area over time then thats a ward so (locked space)<br /> 2. you lock mind attacks to mind not to life (check the locking section in M20 locking section)<br /> 3. In the levitation example if youre not doing that with anything that can miss it needs a lock to autohit. You cant autohit just cause you wana.<br /> 4. As for the cost the place you are citing mentions only sphere lavel not success costs and that is quite standard in the book. That does not mean it does not have a cost as those are generally done by the sphere effect table encouraging STs to think how much would X cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T19:05:58-08:00","id":1548894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548892#post1548892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If ist just an area over time then thats a ward so (locked space)</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Not all area effects are wards. What are you talking about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548892#post1548892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1<br /> 2. you lock mind attacks to mind not to life (check the locking section in M20 locking section)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind was never stated as a pattern sphere. The book always says Forces, Life, Matter and Spirit ( as a pseudo pattern). Also, that's beyond the point I'm trying to make. We can use other spell as an example:<br /> <br /> If you want to give the target the famous &quot;evil eye&quot; with Entropy and curse him with an increased difficulty for all attacks, you don't have to &quot;hit&quot;. You don't need Life to lock into his pattern and there is no dodge. I'm sorry, but I really believe you are wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548892#post1548892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1<br /> 3. In the levitation example if youre not doing that with anything that can miss it needs a lock to autohit. You cant autohit just cause you wana.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you mean by &quot;doing that with anything that can miss&quot;? There ia no &quot;hit&quot; in this spell. You are just affecting reality that is on the range of your sensory abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548892#post1548892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1<br /> 4. As for the cost the place you are citing mentions only sphere lavel not success costs and that is quite standard in the book. That does not mean it does not have a cost as those are generally done by the sphere effect table encouraging STs to think how much would X cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never in M20 they talked about spending successes for locking. Not even in the optional dividing successes rule. If you want to add that to the base successes needed, feel free, but that's not raw at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T23:10:59-08:00","id":1548896,"title":"","content":"M20 512<br /> &quot;512Mage: The Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition<br /> What does that mean? It\u2019s very simple: if you want to alter<br /> someone\u2019s mind, use the Mind Sphere; if you want to alter<br /> her physical body, use the Life Sphere.&quot;<br /> <br /> A area effect that is tied directly to the area is acording to HDYDT a ward. Again its not an issue cause its a inmovable space and an area effect. We are not discussing those now.<br /> <br /> By cant miss i mean you are not for example extending a &quot;invisible tendril&quot; you can control and try to&quot; grab&quot; the target then it autohits (no hit roll) and that requires a lock.<br /> <br /> Yes its never talked about successes for locking then again M20 cant simply codify every magical effect thats why we have the magical effect table to figure that out ourselves. You even were asking yourself why use violence as a catalisator for magic. There are 2 possible answers. 1. It requires locking to do so and 2 its more success expencive. Autohiting is a very powerful thing and should be trated as such. There is a topic here where i ask about locking and there it was sugested to me to use 1 success. At first i opted for 3 (as not needing to hi t again is really powerful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T09:00:52-08:00","id":1548907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548896#post1548896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A area effect that is tied directly to the area is acording to HDYDT a ward. Again its not an issue cause its a inmovable space and an area effect. We are not discussing those now.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. There are tons of examples and possible AoE spells that are <b>not</b> wards and HDYDT never said all area effects are wards. Forces have AoE according to rank.<br /> We are discussing area of effect spells because according to you, a target that enters the area should be able to dodge, and that's not true.<br /> <br /> Please, provide evidence for those claims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548896#post1548896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By cant miss i mean you are not for example extending a &quot;invisible tendril&quot; you can control and try to&quot; grab&quot; the target then it autohits (no hit roll) and that requires a lock.</div> </div> </div> </div>levitation is different than an &quot;invisible force tendril&quot;. Yes, it autohits and no, you don't have to roll an attack Just see the &quot;Telekinesis&quot; or &quot;Embracing the Earth Mother&quot; in revised. They are all just Forces effects affecting the motion of a target. There is no attack roll.<br /> <br /> Also, locking is only necessary if you want to change the location of the spell according to the Pattern. So, if you want to make your target abble to fly, you need to lock with Forces+Life. Just using telekinesis on him is pure Forces 2, manipulating momentum. Locking was <b>never</b> related to attacking. At all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548896#post1548896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes its never talked about successes for locking then again M20 cant simply codify every magical effect thats why we have the magical effect table to figure that out ourselves. You even were asking yourself why use violence as a catalisator for magic. There are 2 possible answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to codify every magical effect. They would just put a line saying it costs X more successes on the spell right there in the locking text in p.511. They didn't. Not there nor anywhere.<br /> <br /> Well, at first I thought that attack based spells would carry over the attack successes into damage (like regular attacks), but then BoS faq removed that idea. So, the only thing left is being easily coincident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548896#post1548896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It requires locking to do so and 2 its more success expencive. Autohiting is a very powerful thing and should be trated as such. There is a topic here where i ask about locking and there it was sugested to me to use 1 success. At first i opted for 3 (as not needing to hi t again is really powerful)</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with your logic is that if you require locking for affecting someone <b>in your sensory range</b> for a damage spell, why wouldn't for all spells? And that's what you are doing, requiring lock for all spells. Which for you, means a whole new sphere rank 2 <b>and</b> 3 more successes on the base roll.<br /> That's completely crazy, starting mages have Arete 1-3.<br /> <br /> Please, answer this example, if you want to give the &quot;evil eye&quot; with Entropy do you need Life as well to &quot;lock&quot; and &quot;autohit&quot;, or do you have to roll an attack, and if thats the case what do you roll?<br /> <br /> What you are arguing is that all spells should have an attack roll to hit and that is not how the game works (never were).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T11:02:15-08:00","id":1548911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548907#post1548907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please, answer this example, if you want to give the &quot;evil eye&quot; with Entropy do you need Life as well to &quot;lock&quot; and &quot;autohit&quot;, or do you have to roll an attack, and if thats the case what do you roll?<br /> <br /> What you are arguing is that all spells should have an attack roll to hit and that is not how the game works (never were).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you do it, if its like the greeks believed that eyes work like rays it requires you to hit the target with the rays. If its the focus on the target then i believe it requires locking.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T12:45:53-08:00","id":1548919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548911#post1548911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how you do it, if its like the greeks believed that eyes work like rays it requires you to hit the target with the rays. If its the focus on the target then i believe it requires locking.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could agree with the first paet, but I would make it a very low diff for attacking (diff 4 or 3, you are literally just looking) and about 9 or 10 do dodge. <br /> <br /> The focus on the target I would ask for some evidence in raw or rotes that base that. On the other hand, I could show several rotes that directly affect the target without any sort of attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T13:51:30-08:00","id":1548923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548919#post1548919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could agree with the first paet, but I would make it a very low diff for attacking (diff 4 or 3, you are literally just looking) and about 9 or 10 do dodge.<br /> <br /> The focus on the target I would ask for some evidence in raw or rotes that base that. On the other hand, I could show several rotes that directly affect the target without any sort of attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said there is no evidence. For me its a logical conclusion that if we have something that can miss and that does not require an attack roll then the later must be more expencive for balance sake and no vulgarity cost is not enough. A desintegrating fist would be still vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T07:34:23-08:00","id":1548950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1548923#post1548923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As i said there is no evidence. For me its a logical conclusion that if we have something that can miss and that does not require an attack roll then the later must be more expencive for balance sake and no vulgarity cost is not enough. A desintegrating fist would be still vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wel, ok.It's a house rule, then. I would rather discuss raw, though. Unfortunately, Mage (Wod) is full of unbalanced stuff. Just take a look at the new M20 foci rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-09T12:32:15-07:00","id":1549110,"title":"","content":"I've learned from experience with clever players that opponents being <i>able </i>to physically dodge some sorts of magical attacks and effects can be used <i>against </i>said opponents, under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Provided that a character knows that they are facing a mage, and that they don't happen to have a sufficiently reliable means of sensing the mystical forces behind magical effects, it's possible to cause an opponent to dive for cover or enact some unneeded defense by doing nothing more than gesticulating madly and shouting in Latin, or something along those lines. Particularly sneaky mages with a good enough understanding of Prime can make this more believable, even to those able to perceive arcane forces, simply by creating a surge of quintessence for an opponent to detect. This would be less likely to fool another mage, especially if they happen to have the right pattern sensing effects &quot;up&quot; such that they can &quot;see&quot; that the mage isn't actually doing anything unusual to the tapestry, but to the uninitiated that's going to look awfully like the mage is about to do <i>something, </i>even if they do have high enough Awareness to reliably sense the use of magic.<br /> <br /> Granted, this can be a very situational thing. It tends to work a lot better in circumstances such that it'd be easy to believe said mage would be desperate enough to risk a vulgar working. Still, an Etherite inspiring an enemy to dive behind a dumpster for dear life by leveling a perfectly mundane laser pointer at them is pretty amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T20:44:31-07:00","id":1549550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548773-dodging-magickal-attacks?p=1549110#post1549110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've learned from experience with clever players that opponents being <i>able </i>to physically dodge some sorts of magical attacks and effects can be used <i>against </i>said opponents, under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Provided that a character knows that they are facing a mage, and that they don't happen to have a sufficiently reliable means of sensing the mystical forces behind magical effects, it's possible to cause an opponent to dive for cover or enact some unneeded defense by doing nothing more than gesticulating madly and shouting in Latin, or something along those lines. Particularly sneaky mages with a good enough understanding of Prime can make this more believable, even to those able to perceive arcane forces, simply by creating a surge of quintessence for an opponent to detect. This would be less likely to fool another mage, especially if they happen to have the right pattern sensing effects &quot;up&quot; such that they can &quot;see&quot; that the mage isn't actually doing anything unusual to the tapestry, but to the uninitiated that's going to look awfully like the mage is about to do <i>something, </i>even if they do have high enough Awareness to reliably sense the use of magic.<br /> <br /> Granted, this can be a very situational thing. It tends to work a lot better in circumstances such that it'd be easy to believe said mage would be desperate enough to risk a vulgar working. Still, an Etherite inspiring an enemy to dive behind a dumpster for dear life by leveling a perfectly mundane laser pointer at them is pretty amusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the thing with awareness. The description talks about detecting magick and recognizing Resonance, which isn't enough for a mage to know what and where an attack is coming from. So, I find this whole spider sense thing a bit of a BS.<br /> <br /> The caster chants in enochian and waves his hand around, how the hell can the target know where to dodge? That's some precog shit, that the ability shouldn't give.<br /> <br /> Since the entry in M20 p.544 talks about &quot;physical attacks&quot; and &quot;can be dodged if that target is capable of dodging the attack in question.&quot; This might imply that a target that has no meaning to know what the fuck is going to happen (and awareness doesn't grant that sort of details) has no way of really dodging said attacks.<br /> <br /> The way I see it is: pointing a plasma gun is ok, the target can jump down. A mage chanting or waving his hands gives no clue of what is going to happen, so I would say that the target is not capable of dodging.<br /> So, in the end, it all depends on the instrument used. And the only advantage of having to roll attack against dodge is to get a coincident effect.<br /> <br /> Another point is that no spell ever required an attack to happen, like telekinesis or Entropy curses. So why wouldn't you also aks for attack rolls for those? If you want transform someone into a goat you don't have to roll attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}